From b57392e9a65ee3d7ec1bf1a01c62ffb02bbd894c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aoripus <1737562@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:26:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: select SPI mode
 for the touchscreen

The Himax HX83121A touch controller on this machine is a cascade IC whose host
interface is selected at runtime by TLMM gpio174: driving it low makes the IC
report raw touch data over SPI, driving it high makes it expose its I2C-HID
interfaces instead.

The boot firmware leaves this pin high, so with the current device tree the IC
stays in I2C-HID mode. The SPI driver still binds and can talk to the IC - the
chip ID is detected and the touch firmware reload is reported - but the IC
never sends touch data and never asserts its level-low interrupt. The
touchscreen is then completely dead, with the interrupt firing only once per
firmware reload.

Describe gpio174 as a low output in the touchscreen's default pin state so it
is already in the SPI configuration before the driver resets the IC and the
firmware is reloaded. The pin only has to be correct before the reload; the IC
latches the mode at that point.

Signed-off-by: aoripus <1737562@qq.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts     | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
index 94e7eeb..bafd88b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -1671,6 +1671,21 @@
 			drive-strength = <2>;
 			bias-disable;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Host-interface select for the Himax HX83121A cascade IC.
+		 * The boot firmware happens to leave this pin high, which puts the IC
+		 * into I2C-HID mode; the IC then accepts SPI register access but never
+		 * reports touch data over SPI and never asserts its interrupt.
+		 * The pin has to be low before the touch firmware reloads.
+		 */
+		mode-n-pins {
+			pins = "gpio174";
+			function = "gpio";
+			drive-strength = <2>;
+			bias-disable;
+			output-low;
+		};
 	};
 
 	uart2_default: uart2-default-state {
-- 
